• T3 is complete and the build is clean.

  **What was built** (all in `frontend/src/components/` + `frontend/src/pages/DashboardPage.tsx`):

  - **FleetPulse** — the signature strip, per BRIEF §3: SVG with one real `<rect>` per device, colour = status, height = freshness (full = just reported, stub = stale over a 15-min window), sorted most-recently-seen left. Hover or arrow-key cursor reveals the device in a caption line (`aria-live`); click/Enter opens the drawer. Status changes get a 1.4 s fade highlight only. A `ResizeObserver` caps tick count and shows "Showing N of M devices" instead of squashing. A status legend row sits under the strip so colour is never the sole carrier.
  - **KpiRow** — total / reporting / needs attention / offline, mono data face with `tabular-nums`.
  - **FilterBar** — site/kind/status native selects composing AND; "Clear filters" only renders while something is active.
  - **QueryPanel** — the 8 pre-defined queries as a selectable list with label, description and live match count. No free-form input anywhere.
  - **DeviceGrid + DeviceCard** — attention-first ordering (critical → good), card shows name, kind icon, StatusBadge (icon + label + colour, always), primary metric, site, last-seen. Empty state uses the BRIEF §8 copy with the real total.
  - **DeviceDrawer** — identity, current readings, recent history list (sparkline marked as T4). Escape and overlay click close it, focus is trapped while open and returned to the trigger on close.

  Charts are left as a clearly marked dashed placeholder section on the page. T1/T2 files and the architecture page were not touched.

  **Build:** `npm run build` → `tsc -b && vite build`, exit 0, zero TypeScript errors under strict mode, zero warnings. Full verbatim output and file list are in `orchestration/logs/T3-SUMMARY.md`.

